\subsection*{Implementation Notes (Phase 4--5)}

\subsubsection*{Theoretical Predictions vs Measured Results}

\begin{table}[H]
\centering
\caption{Predictions vs Measured Results}
{\footnotesize
\begin{tabularx}{\textwidth}{LLL}
\toprule
\textbf{Prediction} & \textbf{Measured} & \textbf{Notes} \\
\midrule
XCM finality ``<2 seconds'' within Polkadot & \textbf{18--32 seconds} (3--5 parachain blocks) & Theoretical estimate did not account for HRMP relay latency through the relay chain. Each hop (sender parachain $\rightarrow$ relay $\rightarrow$ receiver parachain) adds 1--2 blocks \\
XCM cost ``<\$0.002/tx'' & \textasciitilde{}100B tokens per XCM operation & Fee depends on the specific token's exchange rate; the weight-based fee (\textasciitilde{}75--100B tokens due to BlockRatioFee proof\_size scaling) is within the expected range at current testnet valuations \\
Snowbridge as primary bridge & \textbf{Confirmed} --- full Snowbridge v1 deployed and tested E2E & 2 ETH successfully bridged from local Ethereum $\rightarrow$ Bridge Hub $\rightarrow$ AssetHub via beacon light client, relayers, and cryptographic proof verification \\
Hyperbridge as secondary bridge & \textbf{Not implemented} & Deferred to future work --- Snowbridge alone demonstrates the cross-ecosystem bridging thesis \\
Metadata-carrying XCM & \textbf{Implemented differently} --- \texttt{query\_rights\_metadata} emits a \texttt{RightsMetadata} struct as an event, rather than embedding metadata in the XCM payload & XCM payload constraints (\textasciitilde{}4KB) make full metadata embedding impractical; the event-based pattern enables cross-chain consumers to query metadata via XCM \texttt{Transact} \\
Scheduled XCM for auto-renewal & \textbf{Replaced with on-chain scheduler} --- \texttt{on\_initialize} hook processes expired auto-renew subscriptions each block & XCM v5 \texttt{Schedule} instruction is not yet production-ready \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabularx}
}
